  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Water Resource Management in IDP Communities - Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite extensive efforts to improve access to water in Yemen, the country remains one of the most water scarce countries in the world. Depleting natural resources and more frequent cycles of severe weather are making water less available for agricultural and domestic use. The water crisis in Yemen has the potential to contribute to the country&apos;s instability and to further exacerbate existing vulnerabilities faced by host, internally displaced persons, and migrant populations. This three-year program improves the immediate access to water supply, irrigation infrastructure at the watershed level, and community-led resource and conflict management to improve the overall resilience of target communities (with a focus on areas hosting large, displaced populations) to cyclical shocks.</narrative>
  </description>
